{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1401799-new-terrestrial-martial-art-road-warrior-style","id":1401799,"title":"New Terrestrial Martial Art: Road Warrior Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-08T16:12:13-07:00","id":1401799,"title":"New Terrestrial Martial Art: Road Warrior Style","content":"I just finished making this style for a player who wants to use their magitech bike in combat, popping wheelies onto their enemies' faces, side swiping them, ramming them, etc. Based it off of Lightning Hoof Style, but ended up making a lot of mods to it.Thought it might be useful to other games out there, so here it is<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">ROAD WARRIOR STYLE</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">While any number of biker clubs and street gangs might lay claim to this style, in truth it has its roots in the First Age, when the Exalted cultivated down and dirty fighting styles for use with their unintelligent but deadly vehicles. The style has since been forgotten and rediscovered over a hundred different times, as anyone with a taste for the brutal mayhem that is only possible while traveling at fundamentally unsafe speeds aboard vessels with no sense of self preservation will sometimes manifest these Charms out of pure instinct.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Road Warrior Style is an elementally neutral Terrestrial Martial Art. No Dragonblooded aspect needs to spend extra Essence to use its Charms.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"><b>Weapons and Armor:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Warriors who fight with this style can use any weapon with the Reach tag as if it were an unarmed attack. They may use this style while piloting any vehicle that requires Ride to pilot (or Drive, if using the optional rules found in </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Shards of the Exalted Dream</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">), and when making attacks using those vehicles as part of a stunt or ramming maneuver may roll their attack using Martial Arts, ignoring any penalties normally imposed for improvised weapons. Road Warrior martial artists may not wear any armor with a mobility penalty, as it both hinders their movement and betrays a fear of harm that is antithetical to this senselessly reckless style.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"><b>Complementary Abilities:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Most Charms in this style are meant to be used while piloting vehicles that requires Ride to pilot (or Drive, if using the optional rules found in </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Shards of the Exalted Dream</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">). Though they can be activated on foot, they could suffer decreased effectiveness or not work at all. Because a student of this style must clearly be a consummate rider as well as a dedicated martial artist, a practitioner must have a Ride (or Drive) rating equal to the Martial Arts prerequisite listed for each Charm.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">BEAST OF THE ROAD</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> 1m; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Martial Arts 2, Ride 2, Essence 1;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Combo-OK</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> One tick</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Road warriors favor no weapon half so much as the vicious beast of steel and combustion that they ride into battle. Upon activating this Charm, the warrior\u2019s vehicle becomes a weapon that they can wield using (Dexterity + Martial Arts) without a stunt, as they ram and sideswipe their foes. Their vehicle has an Accuracy rating equal to its Maneuverability, a Damage rating equal to its bashing soak, a Rate of 1, and a Defense of 0. Vehicle weapons always deal bashing damage. When used to strike another vehicle, these weapons only suffer superficial damage, and do not follow the usual rules for vehicle crashes.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">On his action, a rider using this Charm can perform any single acrobatic feat from their vehicle without risk of falling. For instance, he could stand on his seat and drive with his feet while aiming a two-handed weapon. The player still needs to make appropriate rolls for the character to perform difficult actions or attacks, but there\u2019s no need for a Ride roll to stay mounted or danger that he will fall off his vehicle. This also eliminates any penalties to the Dodge DV for riding.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">SCREECHING TIRE ASSAULT</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">2m; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Martial Arts 3, Ride 3, Essence 1;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Combo-OK</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Beast of the Road</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Force is mass multiplied by acceleration, and most vehicles have ample amounts of both to spare. Moving for a moment at an almost impossible speed, the character seems set to ram their opponent full force with their vehicle, only to peel inches away at the last second after delivering their attack. Add three dice to the raw damage of an attack made after or during a charge.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">DEAD TO RIGHTS</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">2m per success; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Martial Arts 3, Ride 3, Essence 1;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Combo-OK, Crippling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Fights settled upon the asphalt are contests of speed as well as power, and losing either battle means losing everything. A road warrior may activate this Charm to supplement an attack only during extended contests of speed where they currently have more accumulated successes than their target, using their considerable lead to set up a surprise attack as they slam on the brakes and use their opponent\u2019s own velocity against them. For every one accumulated success the warrior sacrifices in the race\u2019s extended roll, they may add one automatic success to their attack roll. They may convert no more than (Ride or Drive rating) successes in this way per attack.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">ROAD WARRIOR FORM</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">5m; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Martial Arts 4, Ride 4, Essence 2;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Form-type</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">One scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Screeching Tire Assault, Dead to Rights</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">A true road warrior is one with their vehicle. When their deadly chariot burns rubber, the rider leans into the sweet burst of speed. When the warrior needs to evade a bullet or turn a blade, her loyal companion takes the blow for her, and when she needs to strike an enemy down, it lends its weight. Rather than adding one to DV when riding, the rider adds two. Likewise, those suffering close combat attacks from the rider reduce their DVs by two instead of just one. When attacked, the rider chooses whether to direct the attack to herself or to her vehicle in Step 2 of attack resolution, instead of the attacker. As a reminder, all vehicles have a Dodge DV equal to half their Maneuverability, rounded up, and no parry DV.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"><b>STEEL AND THUNDER STRIKE</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">3m; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Martial Arts 4, Ride 4, Essence 2;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Extra Action</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Combo-OK</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Road Warrior Form</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">The character and his ride work together seamlessly as natural partners. When the character attacks a target, his vehicle follows his lead and attacks the same target at the same time. Activating this Charm as part of a flurry, the rider makes any number of actions using the standard flurry rules, then makes a single attack using their vehicle as a weapon (even if </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"><i>Beast of the Road</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> is not active) that ignores their vehicle\u2019s Rate, and does not impose or suffer multiple action penalties. This Charm can be used only when attacking a target that is also a valid target for the vehicle.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">TAKE A WALK</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">4m; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Martial Arts 4, Ride 4, Essence 2;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Combo-OK</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Prerequisite Charms:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Road Warrior Form</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">In a proper death race, warriors are expected to stay with their vehicles until they are either victorious or dead. Stepping foot upon the asphalt for any other reason is the most ignoble kind of defeat a road warrior can suffer. Running alongside her enemy\u2019s vehicle, the warrior leaps across a distance of up to (Martial Arts) yards onto the target\u2019s ride. She then immediately grabs her foe, disentangles him from the wheel and throws him to the ground before leaping back to her vehicle.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Very few vehicles that are piloted using Ride or Drive are adequately-sized for a fight. The warrior\u2019s target suffers a -2 penalty to either DV, unless he is using </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"><i>Beast of the Road </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">or other Charms to make dodging while driving easier. When the character beats her target\u2019s DV, she throws him out of his vehicle. Regardless of whether she succeeds, she leaps back to her mount at the end of her action.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Falling from a vehicle moving more than 10 miles per hour is guaranteed to give the victim a serious case of road rash, which is modeled as a one-time environmental hazard with Trauma and Damage equal to the vehicle\u2019s current speed in miles per hour divided by ten, rounded down. This damage is lethal unless the target lands on soft ground like sand or water, but could potentially have the L tag if they also fell from a great height or onto inherently dangerous terrain.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">NEED A LIFT?</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Cost: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">4m; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Martial Arts 4, Ride 4, Essence 2;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Type:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Keywords:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Combo-Basic</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Duration:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Road Warrior Form</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Whether they\u2019re swinging a blooded brother or sister into the passenger\u2019s seat or grabbing a pencil-necked scrub by the collar and taking them for a memorable ride down the devil\u2019s road, road warriors have many causes to keep their friends and enemies close. This Charm enhances a clinch attack made from the driver\u2019s seat by eliminating any environmental penalties the character would normally suffer on the attempt, especially when driving by at high speeds, and the martial artist gains one automatic success on the attempt. If successfully grappled, the warrior can also swing their target into an open seat of their vehicle as a reflexive action, or just carry them alongside their vehicle, their feet dangling above the asphalt as they travel. They do not need to make (Strength + Athletics) rolls to keep holding their target upright for the rest of the scene, but if the victim escapes the grapple while the warrior is traveling at high speeds then their victim may suffer road rash as is described above.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">FLYING CASKET</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Cost:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\"> 5m; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Mins: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Martial Arts 5, Ride 5, Essence 2;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Type: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Keywords: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Combo-OK</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Duration: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Prerequisite Charms: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">Steel and Thunder Strike, Take A Walk, Need a Lift?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Alegreya\">A true road warrior is loath to damage their most trusted companion, especially in battle, but there is power in this technique. This Charm may supplement a ramming action rolled using (Dexterity + [Ride or Drive]), which if successful causes a crash with a vehicle, person or inanimate object, and does incredibly high damage. The ramming\u2019s target suffers dice of lethal damage equal to the vehicle\u2019s total maximum health levels (including Inoperative and Destroyed levels) if it was a character, or twice that damage if it was another vehicle or inanimate object. The road warrior suffers no damage from this attack, and their vehicle is not automatically totalled, but does suffer dice of unsoakable bashing damage equal to its maximum health levels.</span></span> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 07-08-2020, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}